      <p class="eyebrow">FEATURE AREA 2</p>
      <h3 id="ai-native">AI-native applications and reviews</h3>
      <p>Application intake · Milestone review</p>
      <p>Built with <a href="https://www.simocracy.org/">Simocracy</a></p>
      <p>
        Two processes go AI-native: how projects apply, and how the the projects
        are reviewed. For both project applications and projects milestones, a
        sim does the first pass and a person reviews it and decides if it’s
        cleared for approval. The point is to make the ops side of reviews
        lightweight, for reviewers and for the teams receiving funding.
        Simocracy is
        <a
          href="https://www.filpgf.io/blog/from-funding-history-to-digital-twins-launching-simocracy-for-propgf/"
          >now live in our review process</a
        > and interactions are ongoing.
      </p>

      <div class="rounded-lg border border-line bg-tint p-6">
        <p class="eyebrow">THE TEAM</p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.simocracy.org/">Simocracy</a> is a platform for AI-powered
          governance participation. Someone completes a five-minute interview and
          mints a <strong>sim</strong>: a digital twin with an avatar, a
          constitution that captures their values, and a speaking style.
          Simocracy’s own line is “sims as the engine, humans as the steering
          wheel,” and it has already been used in funding experiments such as
          Funding the Commons.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h4>AI-native application process</h4>
      <p>
        Applications will be pre-populated using existing project information,
        so Kernel teams do not need to resubmit information already on file.
        Teams can review the pre-populated application, make any necessary
        updates, and submit.
      </p>

      <h4>AI-native milestone review</h4>
      <p>
        Sim reviewer assignment and assessment, milestone submission
        notifications to the human reviewer, reminder triggers, and escalation
        flags for reviews that exceed their turnaround time.
      </p>

