      <h2 id="ships">When each feature ships</h2>
      <p>
        Here is what we plan to ship and roughly when, in three delivery
        windows. The roadmap is rolling: we revisit priorities every week, so
        sequencing and dates may shift as we learn from funded teams, reviewers,
        and admins.
      </p>

      <p class="eyebrow">SEP 1 – OCT 31, 2026 · IN PROGRESS</p>
      <h3>Funding framework, transparency &amp; AI-native operations</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Funding metrics everywhere.</strong> Metrics land in cover pages,
          individual project views, and bi-weekly/monthly reporting, and are available
          through Ask Karma. (Metrics &amp; impact)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Simocracy integration v1.</strong> Selection Committee members sims
          are up and running.(Sims &amp; reviews)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automated milestone review.</strong> Sim reviewer assignment and
          assessment, notifications to the human reviewer, reminder triggers, and
          escalation flags for slow reviews. (Sims &amp; reviews)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI-native application process v1.</strong> Application intake, AI-assisted
          application development and review, and a submission workflow. (Applications)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Admin queues live.</strong> Applications, milestones and invoices
          each get a work item with trackable status and age. (Admin operations)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Navigation for the new funding framework.</strong> UX and navigation
          improvements that support the three funding categories. (UX &amp; comms)
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="eyebrow">NOV 1 – DEC 31, 2026 · NEXT</p>
      <h3>Funding ops data &amp; automation</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Keep iterating.</strong> Continued iterations of Simocracy, application
          intake, admin queues, and metrics engagement (Ask Karma, reporting, cover
          pages). (Sims · Apps · Admin · Metrics)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Slack &amp; Telegram integration v1.</strong> Relevant project discussions
          connect to the matching admin work items and project records. (Integrations
          · Admin operations)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Automated project health monitoring.</strong> Flags when a source
          in the metrics dashboard is down or below threshold. (Metrics &amp; impact)
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>AI analytics dashboards for admins.</strong> Admins can sort and
